le, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"e5fCI12X_GLCST668S4ROA","review_id":"0JTc8RRdy-EQfKcba27RZQ","date":"2021-11-13T20:37:31","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9546021223068237,"text_excerpt":"Without a doubt this is a lovely place to have brunch/lunch. It was a nice day in November, so we could sit in the courtyard, which is beautiful. There was music, but they seemed to take a lot of breaks and played very softly, but what we could hear was very pleasant. A very wide buffet, so you can start with salads, shrimp, different breads, then move to about 20 choices ranging from prime rib, to red beans/jambalaya/etoufee, chicken/fish/pasta. I found all the Creole dishes very nice, especially the jambalaya and tried a cup of gumbo for a soup! It is a buffet though, so don't expect individually prepared entrees for your benefit! We had reservations at 12:30 but could still order omele..."},{"business_id":"e5fCI12X_GLCST668S4ROA","review_id":"bp7T1BthTj7hCC0W1rP0VA","date":"2014-08-13T23:36:48","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9475433826446533,"text_excerpt":"This is an excellent brunch location. The brunch buffet is loaded with local favorites. The food was really flavorful. I was a big fan of the turtle soup and the bread pudding. The grits were cooked perfectly; the restaurant had it paired with a veal with gravy. It was delicious. There was an egg station and cold salad bar. The live jazz really added to the old-time feel of the restaurant. Court of Two Sisters is a must if you're in New Orleans."},{"business_id":"e5fCI12X_GLCST668S4ROA","review_id":"CnEeCQd_KKELcrl6V6Y6FA","date":"2017-05-01T18:31:50","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9470973610877991,"text_excerpt":"This place is great! Great ambiance, beautiful/lush courtyard, live music (Daily Jazz Brunch Buffet), and friendly staff. It's a buffet style restaurant. It's nice that way, so you can just get up and pick out what you want to eat. Service can be better, though. It took a while to get our waters and other beverages...and the check. I believe we had to flag down a few servers. It didn't really matter much since the food was too good. I was enjoying myself way too much. It was so hard to choose from everything...and I got full before trying other stuff. If ever you're in town, you should try this place. The entrance is simple, but elegant...I touched the Charm Gate for some luck entering an..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"e5fCI12X_GLCST668S4ROA","photo_id":"vLJhqDJcU_vU7AvwJymNKg","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/vLJhqDJcU_vU7AvwJymNKg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8859395980834961},{"business_id":"e5fCI12X_GLCST668S4ROA","photo_id":"-Eo9mhYzr0TTqJvLLKGZeQ","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/-Eo9mhYzr0TTqJvLLKGZeQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8626073598861694},{"business_id":"e5fCI12X_GLCST668S4ROA","photo_id":"6eQcAkru8I5L61qd5VHXew","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/6eQcAkru8I5L61qd5VHXew.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8482719659805298},{"business_id":"e5fCI12X_GLCST668S4ROA","photo_id":"otuBO8tWLQ9cNWAuFoTgbg","label":"inside","image_url":"/p